jistanidiot@gmail.com wrote:
> So I've died countless times in Sokoban and in the Mines.  I'm
> wondering is it really necessary to do these two branches? 

Depends on your games. I had games without any altar (until the Valley),
and/or without any shops to price-identify things; so had to enter the
mines to make the game progress.

> Sokoban's
> rewards are nice but I'm sure I can find them elsewhere. 

Depends again. There have been games where I had no bag at all (and also
games where not even Sokoban had the bag), in other games it was vice
versa, I found many bags of holding and Sokoban also had one. Then, you
can win the game without reflection (or hope for Medusa's level to get
another source of reflection there). So, yes, you can entirely skip that
level, but in a couple of games it was very convenient to get the price.

